# Environment variables
.env
arcane_dump/
wpak/

# The asset export is NOT disposable and is NOT built here any more. It lives in its own
# repository at C:\code\export_aegisfall -- 4.5 GB, JSON in git and the art in LFS -- and
# `export_aegisfall/` in this checkout is a junction pointing at it. These rules therefore
# no longer mean "throw this away"; they mean "this belongs to the other repo", and they
# keep its 66,581 files from being committed a second time here.
#
# The junction exists because all 32 tools compute REPO_ROOT / "export_aegisfall"
# independently and loop.ps1 keeps its own copy of the path. Delete the link and the next
# loop.ps1 builds a second export inside this repo: two trees, one name, free to disagree.
# Recreate it with:  mklink /J export_aegisfall C:\code\export_aegisfall
export_aegisfall/*
!export_aegisfall/README.md
# The two guides stay tracked here because they are the entry point a fresh integration
# starts from. They are the same bytes the other repo tracks -- the junction means there is
# one physical file, not a copy -- so the two cannot drift.
# Re-including one needs three lines, not one: git will not descend into an excluded
# directory, so `animations/` has to be re-included before anything inside it can be, and
# its contents then excluded again.
!export_aegisfall/animations/
export_aegisfall/animations/*
!export_aegisfall/animations/README.md
export_gltf/
export_icons/
export_textures/
export_atlas/
